{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food","id":948400,"title":"Do Werewolf/Garou use their crinos form to hunt for food?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T23:24:00-07:00","id":948400,"title":"Do Werewolf/Garou use their crinos form to hunt for food?","content":"Also, same goes for all the other breeds. Do they usually use their Crinos form to hunt for food?<br /> <br /> I wonder what they eat? Do their diets consist of Deers or do they go for larger prey like bears?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:55:29-07:00","id":948451,"title":"","content":"Usually? No. (They could, but other forms are probably better suited.)<br /> <br /> Diet? Whatever they want. They're at the top of the food chain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:26:34-07:00","id":948459,"title":"","content":"Hunting in Crinos is kinda problematic, since the Veil is a thing and running around the woods in Crinos all the time is a great way to have some random hiker see you. I can only really imagine it happening if killing something big (like an adult bison) is the only real option for meat and the Garou doesn't want to risk major injury trying to fight it in lupus without a large pack to aid them.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's multiple Level 1 Gifts that let you completely handwave gathering food, so it's likely most Garou are hunting beyond the basic need for sustenance.<br /> <br /> And wolves, while carnivores, aren't terribly picky and are very adaptable (some wild packs seem to solely go after big game, while others focus on lots of small game, and some change with seasonal migrations, etc.). Garou are even better because they can always eat in homid and survive as an omnivore even in the wilderness away from simple human food sources. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:40:26-07:00","id":948461,"title":"","content":"Can wolves eat plants though. They have to eat raw meat right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:04:35-07:00","id":948473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948461#post948461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can wolves eat plants though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948461#post948461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have to eat raw meat right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Wolves prefer meat, but can and will eat plant matter if that's what's available.<br /> <br /> Werewolves (and other shapeshifters), being spiritual hybrids of animal and human, will certainly have cultural preferences, but are omnivores.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:36:44-07:00","id":948565,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Topic moved to appropriate sub-forum.\u200b</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:00:36-07:00","id":948573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948461#post948461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can wolves eat plants though. They have to eat raw meat right?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Russia farmes even shot wolves for eating their beets when there was nothing else to hunt.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that garou do not usually hunt in Crinos form, if they hunt animals for food.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:54:38-07:00","id":948607,"title":"","content":"Well, it would be more efficient to eat in human or wolf form because of the smaller size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:45:06-07:00","id":948684,"title":"","content":"This is just my headcanon, but I think a lot of lupus view using anything above lupus in hunting a bit like someone bringing a mini-gun to a deer hunt. It's needlessly excessive and kills the sacredness of the act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:55:43-07:00","id":948693,"title":"","content":"It said in the first edition Red Talon Tribal book that to earn the rite to breed, a red talon must fairly win the position of alpha, and must fight all competitors with no use of Gifts or other garou abilitys, and if defeated, he must go elsewhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:08:12-07:00","id":948729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948693#post948693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It said in the first edition Red Talon Tribal book that to earn the rite to breed, a red talon must fairly win the position of alpha, and must fight all competitors with no use of Gifts or other garou abilitys, and if defeated, he must go elsewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man just like real wolves! Who would have known!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:27:23-07:00","id":948745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948729#post948729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh man just like real wolves! Who would have known!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought it was appropiate to the subject at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:47:55-07:00","id":948770,"title":"","content":"Cultural context of tribes (particularly those people may not be familiar with) is always relevant. I'd imagine that black spirals hunt in homid as they likely enjoy eating man flesh. Bone gnawers likely hunt dumpsters and human food sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:34:18-07:00","id":948812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948770#post948770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cultural context of tribes (particularly those people may not be familiar with) is always relevant. I'd imagine that black spirals hunt in homid as they likely enjoy eating man flesh. Bone gnawers likely hunt dumpsters and human food sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO it can also depend on breed. Homid - Mostly what humans always eat. Lupus, try for meat mostly, but veg will do in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:05:08-07:00","id":948886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948812#post948812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO it can also depend on breed. Homid - Mostly what humans always eat. Lupus, try for meat mostly, but veg will do in a pinch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Hunting in Crinos would be inefficient anyways. Hunting in lupus is generally faster. And If you have something really large you need to take down for hunger reasons, switching to Hispo is generally a better option since it's still faster than Crinos form (from memory) with comparable stats.<br /> I suppose I could see a younger Homid switching to Crinos instead of Hispo to fight a bear or something once he/she has run it down in another form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T16:28:20-07:00","id":948923,"title":"","content":"Oh how do you think Lupus who arent Talons will feel about trying Human cuisine as a bit of experimentation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T16:54:30-07:00","id":948937,"title":"","content":"Most of them have foraged for scraps, so they are familiar with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:30:11-07:00","id":948958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948473#post948473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Wolves prefer meat, but can and will eat plant matter if that's what's available.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... <i>sort of</i>. Wolves <i>are</i> carnivores. They <i>will</i> sometimes eat plant matter (for instance your dog eating grass), but they cannot <i>subsist</i> on it. Their gastrointestinal tract is incapable of digesting certain things that true omnivores (like humans for instance) can -- particularly certain grains. Most importantly however, their entire biology and metabolism is designed for a fairly protein-rich diet, so they're not going to do well without a fairly robust proportion of meat in their diet.<br /> <br /> That said, they <i>do</i> enjoy non-meat items. French farmers in the region adjoining the Pyrenees Mountains generally have to have guard dogs to ward off marauding wolves -- not to keep them away from their flocks, however. They need the dogs to protect their <i>vineyards</i> -- the wolves of the Pyrenees apparently think grapes are a delicious treat. There's actually video somewhere of them raiding a vineyard and delicately pulling bunches of grapes off the vines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T18:33:44-07:00","id":948987,"title":"","content":"Great Pyranees are great dogs by the way, though they are as stubborn as everything. I wonder if any Garou reproduce with them (Bone Gnawers do anything and I could see members of the Children of Gaia doing them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-11-2016, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:18:06-07:00","id":949050,"title":"","content":"I imagine Black Spirals do hunt in Crinos, since that is most of them's breed form, cause they love inspiring fear, they love mayhem, they are batshit crazy and don't much care bout the Veil, and that its easier to eat a human head that way<br /> <br /> Snap, crackle, pop, its delicious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 08-11-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:23:41-07:00","id":949054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948987#post948987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Great Pyranees are great dogs by the way, though they are as stubborn as everything. I wonder if any Garou reproduce with them (Bone Gnawers do anything and I could see members of the Children of Gaia doing them).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would take an <b>extremely</b> desperate Gnawer to consider such a thing, and even then I don't really see it happening. No other Garou would ever consider it. Even Spirals wouldn't normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:23:59-07:00","id":949055,"title":"","content":"I think Garou will probaly hunt in Crinos if it is the ONLY way they see to avoid starvation... before their extinction, Im sure a Garou pack took down a wooly mammonth or two that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:28:56-07:00","id":949058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=949050#post949050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Black Spirals do hunt in Crinos, since that is most of them's breed form, cause they love inspiring fear, they love mayhem, they are batshit crazy and don't much care bout the Veil, and that its easier to eat a human head that way<br /> <br /> Snap, crackle, pop, its delicious</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirals do uphold the veil though. It's a matter of self preservation. That is one of the only tenets that both Litanys have in common. I can see Spirals killing in Crinos just fine, but for actual hunting, almost all of the other forms are better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=949055#post949055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Garou will probaly hunt in Crinos if it is the ONLY way they see to avoid starvation... before their extinction, Im sure a Garou pack took down a wooly mammonth or two that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that, but again it would be the fight that might take place in Crinos, not really the hunt. Crinos is suited for combat. Lupus would be best for hunting, followed (far behind) by Hispo.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:35:04-07:00","id":949062,"title":"","content":"For Black Spirals if not Crino, then in my opinion it would Hispo, again the fear and the mayhem is what they would,be after. Sure a pack of wolves is scary coming after you. But a pack of Wargs is even scarier. I can see BSD using lupus to search for prey, but once they have the trail I can see them going hispo to chase it in a corner and then Crinos when its cornered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:43:46-07:00","id":949136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948937#post948937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948923#post948923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh how do you think Lupus who arent Talons will feel about trying Human cuisine as a bit of experimentation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them have foraged for scraps, so they are familiar with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they were treated as a house pet prior to their shifting, they've probably been fed table scraps anyway..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:33:01-07:00","id":949188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948987#post948987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great Pyranees are great dogs by the way, though they are as stubborn as everything. I wonder if any Garou reproduce with them (Bone Gnawers do anything and I could see members of the Children of Gaia doing them).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By canon no, if its ever been domesticated its.. &quot;Done&quot; for kinfolk. Personally I'm more ok with Feral Dogs being &quot;close enough&quot; since friggen Dingo are. Just as long as its not a stupid breed(no werepoodles)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:03:10-07:00","id":949260,"title":"","content":"Would a Dog Shapeshifter be a creature of the Weaver then? Or would it be one of the Mockery Breeds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:08:45-07:00","id":949265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=949136#post949136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if they were treated as a house pet prior to their shifting, they've probably been fed table scraps anyway..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of wolf kinfolk, are &quot;Semitame&quot; according to some line I remember reading been years though.<br /> <br /> They have some kind of positive experience with human kinfolk, in their first few weeks<br /> <br /> but are NOT repeat not, house pets<br /> <br /> This is probaly not the case, if their being raised in a place where the tribe is uncertain of their ability to protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:00:43-07:00","id":949314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=949260#post949260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Dog Shapeshifter be a creature of the Weaver then? Or would it be one of the Mockery Breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What is a Dog Shapeshifter? There are multiple Garou groups who's &quot;lupus&quot; breed is a type of wild dog. African Talons, Australian Talons, the Singing Dogs who didn't fit into any tribe in Rage across the world. Even purely wild breed wolves in North america for the most part have a fairly large percentage of Coyote in them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand what would an Inugami be....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:43:40-07:00","id":949334,"title":"","content":"theirs the Warwolves an early mockery breed not even sapient, that often times are of dog extraction created to consume garou and their kinfolk...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:38:51-07:00","id":949542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=948987#post948987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great Pyranees are great dogs by the way, though they are as stubborn as everything. I wonder if any Garou reproduce with them (Bone Gnawers do anything and I could see members of the Children of Gaia doing them).</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition this was not uncommon... to the point I think there's a picture in a sourcebook of a spaniel-looking Gnawer NPC. Then somewhere in either late 2nd or early revised it was retcon'ed to &quot;Nuh uh, no, never. It has to be a wolf. Not just a wolf, but a WILD wolf. 100% pure, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then later on they started introducing a half dozen other not-wolf breeds... because screw it. By now I don't see why they don't reintroduce Dog-Gnawers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:20:21-07:00","id":949602,"title":"","content":"Yes, there has always been some ambivalence, since dogs are wolves, just with the juvenile traits amped to maximum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:23:42-07:00","id":949650,"title":"","content":"The reason to include a wider array of wild canids, and not include domesticated dogs, is pretty simple: spirit rules are what runs this.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't generally care about human scientific taxonomy. They form broods and courts according to their natures. Dog isn't a Weaver spirit, but Dog has separated from Wolf spiritually to the point where Dog no longer has sufficient connection to the Garou. Meanwhile animals like the maned wolf (which is not a &quot;true&quot; wolf by not being a member of the <i>Canis</i> species), are still spiritually part of the Wolf brood and count as wolf enough for the Garou to have a connection to.<br /> <br /> The same reason why coyotes, which are known to hybridize with wolves in the wild, don't turn into Garou. Coyote and Wolf are separate spirits and Coyote's children are the Nuwisha.<br /> <br /> The books don't do a great job of being consistent in application of these principles, but there is a solid framework there to explain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:40:23-07:00","id":950136,"title":"","content":"So, would a red wolf, which is something like 50%-75% Coyote, be Garou Kin or Nuwisha Kin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:27:25-07:00","id":950157,"title":"","content":"Again, the genetically X% one doesn't matter. Dogs are 100% wolf genetically.<br /> <br /> By the current rules, things go to the mother (probably just for ease, you always know who the mother is, and it's a far simpler rule than most other options). Which means coywolf and red wolf populations are going to have both Garou and Nuwisha kin in them, because at least some of the hybridization is going to go in both directions. That said, they're probably more Garou kin than Nuwisha kin in those populations, because there's more Garou than Nuwisha competing for the same kin, and the Nuwisha aren't likely to pick a fight with the Garou over red wolves when full coyote clans aren't having the same population issues as wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T12:59:14-07:00","id":950187,"title":"","content":"Well, there are around 100 Nuwushi and around 15,000 Garou on Earth. Even if Nuwisha hump every coyote they come across (or red wolf), it will really not matter. That being said, coyote populations have been growing for the past two hundred years, so there should be more Nuwisha than there are Garou (then again, the same could be said about Gurahl because there are five times as many black bears in North America than wolves globally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T02:43:18-07:00","id":950486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=949650#post949650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason to include a wider array of wild canids, and not include domesticated dogs, is pretty simple: spirit rules are what runs this.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't generally care about human scientific taxonomy. They form broods and courts according to their natures. Dog isn't a Weaver spirit, but Dog has separated from Wolf spiritually to the point where Dog no longer has sufficient connection to the Garou. Meanwhile animals like the maned wolf (which is not a &quot;true&quot; wolf by not being a member of the <i>Canis</i> species), are still spiritually part of the Wolf brood and count as wolf enough for the Garou to have a connection to.<br /> <br /> The same reason why coyotes, which are known to hybridize with wolves in the wild, don't turn into Garou. Coyote and Wolf are separate spirits and Coyote's children are the Nuwisha.<br /> <br /> The books don't do a great job of being consistent in application of these principles, but there is a solid framework there to explain it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's a solid framework we are not really given. And then there's stuff in the CB book about how domestication &quot;kills&quot; a kinfolk status for Grondir and Apis. Then Shattered dream tried to reintroduce the idea that a certain number of generations of not breeding true cancels out any chance of kinfolkness to explain why all of humanity isn't kinfolk came off as just odd.<br /> <br /> <br /> My Dog gnawer rule is if its big and wolfy looking and feral it can count. NO small dogs, no stupidly bred dogs. Its purely built on visual concept but that's just as much a solid frame work that I can totally say is &quot;spiritual reality&quot; as Dingo Lupus counting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:06:39-07:00","id":950647,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think that a Chihuahua Garou would be ludicrous. I think a Great Pyrenees Garou or Newfoundland Garou could work, though they would be physically stronger though more fragile than Wolf Garou (I would increase their Strength by one but reduce their Stamina by one for every non-human form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:48:16-07:00","id":950669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=950647#post950647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I think that a Chihuahua Garou would be ludicrous. I think a Great Pyrenees Garou or Newfoundland Garou could work, though they would be physically stronger though more fragile than Wolf Garou (I would increase their Strength by one but reduce their Stamina by one for every non-human form).</div> </div> </div> </div>My dog Luna, as seen in my profile pic, is definitely wolf enough for that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:56:45-07:00","id":950677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=950647#post950647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I think that a Chihuahua Garou would be ludicrous. I think a Great Pyrenees Garou or Newfoundland Garou could work, though they would be physically stronger though more fragile than Wolf Garou (I would increase their Strength by one but reduce their Stamina by one for every non-human form).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going to allow Big Dogs to be bred into Garou than I think there are other things to consider besides stats. A Great Pyrenees Garou or Newfoundland Garou certainly wouldn't be able to long run (or have significant trouble with it). And they would have to be limited to Bone Gnawers. And I'm not sure why you think those breeds are stronger than Wolves. Garou already represent larger wolves. I think having a dog-bred Garou would only have inferior stats. I would probably just give them 1 less Dex bonus and higher dif (+2 or 3 maybe) to long-running and maybe all other non soak Stamina rolls. All told, maybe just make the idea a 3-5 point Bone Gnawer flaw. Haven't really given it much thought, so I don't know what other drawbacks there would be. If just the stuff above, maybe the flaw would only be 3 points. The social implications would be fairly terrible, but Gnawers already suffer the bulk of those. They would essentially be the lowest standing Garou in the already lowest Tribe of Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:56:52-07:00","id":950678,"title":"","content":"Of course, Garou are actually dogs in their own way, with a hybrid mentality of human and wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:02:33-07:00","id":950707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=950678#post950678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, Garou are actually dogs in their own way, with a hybrid mentality of human and wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a dog, that's a wolf who's also some guy you know, who is often ready to kill you at a moment's notice. Rage makes for a vast difference from human and wolf both, and ensures that the Garou aren't like dogs at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:35:02-07:00","id":950723,"title":"","content":"<i>Mutter</i><br /> <br /> OK, I had a bigger post, browser crashed, here's the short response:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=950486#post950486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a solid framework we are not really given.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might not have an official W20 answer, but this framework was laid out explicitly in the Revised ST Handbook and the statements in CB20 and Shattered Dreams are completely in line with that canon statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My Dog gnawer rule is if its big and wolfy looking and feral it can count. </div> </div> </div>Feral is more interesting, because there isn't a solid definition of when a line of dogs can be considered truly feral. While a good number of domesticated animals (cats, goats, and pigs are great examples) not only go feral quickly, they also go feral to the point where it will take a few generations to redomesticate them even from a line that all came from purely domestic animals.<br /> <br /> Dogs, are weird. Dogs take to &quot;free-range&quot; living quickly enough, and revert to wild behaviors when they do (though urban free-range dogs often adopt highly specialized unique behaviors). However, they can be brought back into domestication just as easily. It usually takes multiple generations of free-range dog breeding without humans to result in truly feral dogs that can't be reintroduced to living humans. In that time, almost all of those populations revert to a more wild-type physical expression; if for no other reasons that most highly bred dog breeds can't actually survive in the wild for multiple generations between issues like inability to give live births or being so big they can't hunt enough to sustain their metabolic needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:52:11-07:00","id":950729,"title":"","content":"Or the fact that cross breeding removes the majority of the special traits. I am not quite sure which dog breeds you are talking about, all of my dogs had puppies born without difficulties, so you must be talking about very small breeds. Large dogs can survive as ferals, I have encountered more than a few down south, but they will breed with anything, including coyotes, and the resulting pups will be small if the mother is small. Since more small dogs can survive in a territory than large dogs, small ferals will quickly outbreed large ferals, making the majority of the population small ferals after a few dog generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:41:28-07:00","id":950839,"title":"","content":"All of the toy breeds have gotten to the point where the breed cannot be maintained without human medical intervention during birth. Some individuals can, but the majority can't. A good number of the small breeds have gotten to this point as well.<br /> <br /> There's also the brachycephalic breeds of any size, whether the breathing problems are issues from birth and on. Even the large breeds that have such snouts would struggle to survive in the wild. On the birth side of it, the pups can have trouble breathing even with simulation, and the mother can go into distress with a difficult birth.<br /> <br /> And the breeds where hip dsyplasia is common can impact birth canal function; which is also independent of size.<br /> <br /> I'm also assuming you really mean medium dogs (which is the general category that is what most people think of as &quot;normal&quot; dog/wolf/coyote size) taking over, since small breed dogs struggle in the wild as other predators will target them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:16:27-07:00","id":950856,"title":"","content":"Yes, I am used to large breeds, so I consider normal sized dogs to be small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:22:04-07:00","id":963875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=950677#post950677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think having a dog-bred Garou would only have inferior stats...</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit off topic, but... To make things interesting, I created a non-canon tribe of weredogs (who are distinct from the Garou). I've got a whole backstory on why they were created, and why the Garou haven't noticed them yet. But as part of the general plot, they start out with extremely inferior capabilities when compared to the Garou. Among other things, they have no Rage, can't step sideways, and (because of the spirits' hostility) as a practical matter can't get anyone to teach them gifts. On the other hand, they have major advantages over the Garou in some respects. They have no Curse, they can include ordinary humans in their packs (which also immunizes them to the Delirium), as well as a bunch of other little goodies. They can also wander around in broad daylight in their Canis (equivalent to Lupus) form without drawing any attention whatsoever.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot the best part: Lacking Rage, despite being lunar-aspected, they have no vulnerability to silver -- much akin to the Nuwisha. Ghouls, fomori, First Teams, and what have you who try to take on a pack of weredogs (invariably mistaking them for Garou) find themselves unexpectedly facing rather significant tactical challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-05-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:10:43-07:00","id":963903,"title":"","content":"I think I read that at one point, it was an interesting read. I've been kicking around using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:55:16-07:00","id":963927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=963875#post963875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit off topic, but... To make things interesting, I created a non-canon tribe of weredogs (who are distinct from the Garou). I've got a whole backstory on why they were created, and why the Garou haven't noticed them yet. But as part of the general plot, they start out with extremely inferior capabilities when compared to the Garou. Among other things, they have no Rage, can't step sideways, and (because of the spirits' hostility) as a practical matter can't get anyone to teach them gifts. On the other hand, they have major advantages over the Garou in some respects. They have no Curse, they can include ordinary humans in their packs (which also immunizes them to the Delirium), as well as a bunch of other little goodies. They can also wander around in broad daylight in their Canis (equivalent to Lupus) form without drawing any attention whatsoever.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot the best part: Lacking Rage, despite being lunar-aspected, they have no vulnerability to silver -- much akin to the Nuwisha. Ghouls, fomori, First Teams, and what have you who try to take on a pack of weredogs (invariably mistaking them for Garou) find themselves unexpectedly facing rather significant tactical challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to post all of the Cha Creation rules on them??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T17:01:04-07:00","id":963976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=963927#post963927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Care to post all of the Cha Creation rules on them??</div> </div> </div> </div>Character creation hasn't been finalized yet. What I've got thus far goes to around 80 pages, but most of that is background stuff (creation myth, social structure, camps, relations with humanity, etc.). Moreover, I'm still in what I call &quot;mental-dump-mode&quot; and much of what I have is in dire need of editing (which will happen once I'm comfortable that I have every potential good idea down).<br /> <br /> Basic character creation will be as follows:<br /> <br /> Attributes: 7/5/3<br /> Abilities: 13/9/5<br /> Advantages: Backgrounds 5<br /> Finishing Touches: Gnosis 1, Willpower 4, Rank 0 (&quot;pup&quot;), freebie points 15. (Currently we're discussing making it 21 freebie points -- arguments being made for and against).<br /> <br /> Gnosis is simply for certain reflexive rolls (resisting vampiric embrace, for instance) and cannot be consciously used at character creation. Form statistics are the same as for the Garou, and forms are referred to by the same names except for the Lupus equivalent which the weredogs call &quot;Canis&quot;. Weredogs cannot purchase the following Backgrounds: Ancestors ( although that's also under discussion), Fetish, Kinfolk, Mentor, Pure Breed, Rites, or Totem. Weredogs <i>may </i>purchase Paths in Hedge Magic, and may do so as any human sorcerer would <i>without</i> suffering the experience point penalty that Garou do. Weredogs have no Gifts at character creation, and gaining Gifts and Rites is intentionally hampered by the setting. Weredogs regaining the use of either Gifts or Rites should be the focus of an entire chronicle (weredogs are no longer party to the Great Spirit Pact, and the spirits are generally hostile).<br /> <br /> Other important points are that a weredog's Crinos form does not inflict the Delirium. The Veil still applies, but only to a degree. All human observers generally remember the event, but will rationalize. More humans remember everything about the encounter and are less likely to rationalize than if it were a Garou (discussions are going on about giving witnesses between a +3 to +5 bonus on the Delirium chart as to whether they rationalize or remember). Moreover, as humans recognize weredogs as protectors on a subconscious level, weredogs have a strange anti-Delirium effect when in Crinos. If the number of Garou (or other shapeshifters) in Crinos in a scene is less than double the number of weredogs in Crinos in that scene, the Delirium is negated (the Veil is not).<br /> <br /> So, that's basically character creation in a furry nutshell. We (my gaming circle and I) are only now beginning to get around to the nuts and bolts of character creation, however. For instance, as the weredogs are barred from most Backgrounds, we're coming up with replacements. Most are shamelessly plagiarized from other WoD books, but the following is an example of an original one:<br /> (I'm putting this in &quot;Spoiler&quot; brackets so I don't create an obnoxious &quot;wall of text&quot;)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>PACK BONDS</b><br /> Like their lupine cousins, dogs are also highly sociable creatures with elaborate, cooperative social structures. As such, the weredogs, like the Garou, also share a spiritual link with their packmates. However, just as wolves and dogs differ from each other (particularly where humans are involved), werewolves\u2019 and weredogs\u2019 Pack Bonds operate in slightly different ways.<br /> One of the most obvious ways that a werewolf\u2019s ties to his packmates differs from that of a weredog cousin, is that the Garou link with their packs by means of a pack totem. Rather than linking directly to each other, the totem serves as the spiritual locus of the pack and the various packmates link directly to the totem and by extension, indirectly <i>through</i> the totem. Weredogs, being much more tied to the physical world and with far more tenuous links to the spirit world, do not form packs this way. Weredog packmates link directly to each other.<br /> The next way that the two differ is in just who can be a party to a weredog pack. Just as dogs often form extremely tight bonds to humans, weredog packs are likewise far less choosy about who counts as a packmate. As such, ordinary dogs and normal humans can join a weredog pack (and benefit from Pack Bonds).<br /> Lastly, the strength of a werewolf pack\u2019s bonds is determined by the pack as a whole. As weredogs link directly to each other without need of a totem, the strength of the bonds between specific packmates determine how the Pack Bonds work on a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> Pack Bonds (at least for a weredog pack) are a complicated issue, with many distinct parts. Pack Bonds also represent perhaps the greatest \u201cmagic\u201d powers the weredogs have. <br /> First off, a weredog pack can be thought of as having four distinct elements: First and most important are the actual weredogs themselves. This block determines how large the various other blocks may be, and by extension how large the pack as a whole may become. The next element are the humans in the pack (if any). The pack may have as many humans as there are weredogs (so a pack with three weredogs may also have up to three humans). The third element are the dogs in the pack (if any). Again, the pack may have as many dogs in it as it has weredogs. The last element are the supernaturals in the pack (if any). Weredog packs can include just about any sort of supernatural being imaginable. Wraiths, Changelings, Vampires, Mages, Werewolves, Garou Kinfolk, Ghouls, and other Changing Breeds are all potential packmates. The pack may have as many supernaturals in it as it has weredogs. So a pack that has five weredogs could theoretically have up to twenty packmates (though this is unlikely as non-weredog supernatural packmates are extremely rare).<br /> Non-weredogs are subject to certain restrictions. The potential packmate-to-be must both implicitly trust all the existing members of the pack and, in turn be implicitly trusted <i>by</i> the pack before the Pack Bonds will slip into place. A human intending to infiltrate the pack by feigning friendship will <i>never</i> establish the connection necessary to bond with the pack. Likewise, if any member of the pack is suspicious or in any way distrusts the potential new packmate, the bonding will also fail.<br /> Potential recruits cannot be bonded in any way to anyone or anything outside the pack or the Pack Bonds will not fall into place. Humans or Ghouls who have been blood-bonded, Garou with pre-existing Pack Bonds (any dots whatsoever in Totem), Hegenyokai bonded to a sentai, or any other similar situation make it impossible to bond to a weredog pack.<br /> If (through combat or accident) the number of weredogs in the pack falls below the number needed to sustain the total in any of the other three elements, the excess number of non-weredogs are <i>not</i> lost. Rather, no new non-weredogs may join the pack (including remaining elements that are not over-populated) until either a new weredog joins the pack, or a member of the over-populated element leaves (or is killed) and the pack is again back in balance.<br /> <br /> One of the most devastating things about Garou packs is their capacity to perform pack tactics. Weredog packs may use pack tactics just like Garou do, although in practice, this works a little different.<br /> First, any member of the pack who wishes to participate in pack tactics must have at least one dot in Pack Bonds to do so. Secondly, the number of pack tactics that can be accomplished has nothing whatsoever to do with Gnosis (a good thing since weredogs generally don\u2019t have that). Third, pack tactics are learned by individual members, <i>not</i> the pack as a whole. Fourth, for two (or more) packmates to perform a pack tactic, all participating members must know that particular pack tactic. Fifth, the total number of pack tactics an individual member can know is equal to his number of dots in Pack Bonds (whenever a new dot in Pack Bonds is picked up, the player should annotate what pack tactic his character wishes to learn).<br /> Some non-weredog packmates are severely restricted in what pack tactics they may participate in. Specifically, some pack tactics require participants to be in certain forms or require the superhuman speed and strength of a hybrid form. For example, a human packmate <i>could</i> learn Fur Gnarl. However, he would not be able to participate in the opening move (which requires claws or fangs). He <i>could</i> however, take part in the second move (by using a rifle to target the newly vulnerable patch on the pack\u2019s adversary, for example). Which pack tactics (or which elements of a pack tactic) may be used by a packmate is entirely at the discretion of the Storyteller, and should make sense given non-shapeshifters\u2019 limitations.<br /> <br /> (To avoid confusion, the following term is used: Just because two weredogs are part of a pack does not mean that either or both have any dots in Pack Bonds. For the purposes of this subject, \u201cpackmates\u201d refers to any member of the pack with a number of dots in Pack Bonds equal to or greater than the character in question.)<br /> <br /> The following are the powers that are associated with each level in the Background. Generally, these powers function only with packmates who have at least that rating in Pack Bonds. For instance, a member of a pack has one dot in Pack Bonds and another has three. The two packmates can only use the powers with each other afforded by one dot in Pack Bonds. If however, another packmate has four dots, then the packmate with three dots can make use of all powers of one, two and three-dot levels with that packmate (and vice-versa), while the one-dot packmate may use only the powers of one-dot level with <i>both</i> his three-dot and four-dot packmates. The four-dot packmate may <i>not</i> use any of his four-dot powers until one of his packmates gets at least four dots in Pack Bonds (and then <i>only</i> with that packmate).<br /> <br /> \u25cf In the event of an ambush or a surprise of any sort, if any packmate succeeds in the Perception + Alertness, or Wits + Primal Urge roll and the surprise fails, all packmates are assumed to have succeeded at the roll (even those not capable of making the roll). All packmates are aware if a packmate is wounded or in distress (though not the packmate\u2019s location). Characters normally vulnerable to the Delirium (such as most humans) are now immune.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf All packmates\u2019 general direction and vague distance are known. If a packmate is wounded, the extent of his injuries is roughly known.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf All packmates\u2019 general locations are known. Packmates can send simple instructions or requests to other packmates (\u201cgo there\u201d or \u201cattack that one\u201d) as a free action. Any packmate whose initiative roll is lower than that of the pack alpha (assuming the alpha is engaged in the combat), or that of whoever is leading the combat (if not the alpha), may use that leader\u2019s initiative roll as if it was their own. The exact injuries of all wounded packmates are known.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf All packmates\u2019 exact locations are known. Packmates may silently communicate with each other through their pack bonds (restricted to simple concepts as if they were communicating in the dog-tongue \u2013 across any distance). Mental pictures, the sound of a target\u2019s voice, and a prey\u2019s scent may also be shared. A single Knowledge, Skill, or Talent may be shared with a packmate (although not while it\u2019s owner is simultaneously using it). Another packmate\u2019s wound penalties may be temporarily absorbed (multiple packmates may absorb part of the wounded packmate\u2019s total, effectively spreading out the wound penalties across the rest of the pack).<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Packmates may silently speak to each other through their pack bonds over any distance as if they were face to face (effectively mental telepathy). Packmates may allow a packmate to see through their eyes, hear through their ears, smell through their nose and otherwise fully share any or all of their senses. Any single Attribute may be shared with a packmate (although not while its owner is simultaneously using it \u2013 the form modifiers of the owner do <i>not</i> transfer however, only the base rating). Packmates may absorb a wound level per turn into themselves (even aggravated wounds), essentially sacrificing themselves to heal their packmates. This means that a weredog may absorb the lethal damage done to a human packmate, and then heal it using his regeneration (another peculiarity of this is that a werewolf packmate may absorb the wounds of a human packmate who is shot with silver, and regenerate it as it is merely lethal damage, not aggravated). By spending a number of Willpower points, an equal number of points of a packmate\u2019s Rage may be absorbed for a day. Only packmates who do not naturally possess Rage may absorb such points. The Rage points may not be used by the one who absorbed it. The packmate who absorbed the Rage points may give them back at any time before the full day has elapsed (its owner has no say in this), although the Willpower spent is not returned. Alternately, the Rage points\u2019 owner may pull upon them at any time and regain the full total. After a day, the Rage points return to their owner unless a packmate spends more Willpower to absorb them again. This power generally goes unused as most packmates have no Rage, but should a Garou or member of the Changing Breeds join the pack (for whatever reason), it allows the pack to temporarily relieve their packmate of the debilitating effects of Rage (including The Curse).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> As you can see much of this needs serious editing. Also, some of this seems seriously over-powered, so as our discussions continue, some of these things are going to get pared down a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:53:46-07:00","id":964010,"title":"","content":"I'd say if a Dog has reclaimed its &quot;wolfness&quot;, then the dog is spiritually attuned enough for Garou breeding. Buck from Call of the Wild could have Garou Descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:22:28-07:00","id":964061,"title":"","content":"I would actually just have a were-dog being an outcast Garou. They are the same species as gray wolves. I would just say that selective breeding removed the Garou 'gene' and that it can be reintroduced by having Garou or wolf Kinfolk breed into the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:58:11-07:00","id":964074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=964061#post964061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually just have a were-dog being an outcast Garou. They are the same species as gray wolves. I would just say that selective breeding removed the Garou 'gene' and that it can be reintroduced by having Garou or wolf Kinfolk breed into the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting is better off without anything akin to &quot;Garou gene&quot; ever being uttered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:57:30-07:00","id":964090,"title":"","content":"That's a nice write up.. Though with so many backrounds forbidden, there's not much left for them. You have Allies, pack, and resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T01:42:16-07:00","id":964155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=964090#post964090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though with so many backrounds forbidden, there's not much left for them. You have Allies, pack, and resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Contacts, Rank, Equipment, Fame, Influence, and (toying with) Camp. Remember, I said we're still playing with Resources, and Numina is also sort of like a Background. Work in progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-06-2016, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T13:07:25-07:00","id":964486,"title":"","content":"Equipment is not a standard garou allowed backround, same with influence and fame iirc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:56:14-07:00","id":965488,"title":"","content":"Equipment is an odd background. Quite honestly, a character should invest in Arsenal, Fetish, or Resources instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:34:19-07:00","id":965844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=964486#post964486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Equipment is not a standard garou allowed backround, same with influence and fame iirc...</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but weredogs (or at least the weredogs as I'm writing them) aren't standard Garou. Actually, they technically <i>aren't</i> Garou.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Equipment is an odd background. Quite honestly, a character should invest in Arsenal, Fetish, or Resources instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my write up on Equipment, I actually briefly mention why Equipment is the Background weredogs use, rather than Arsenal. The weredogs (again, as I'm writing them) are seriously focused on staying off the authorities' radar. Equipment is not just cool stuff, but the legal authority to possess it. Arsenal is the survivalist/gun-nut with a rocket launcher in his attic (think Sarah Connor and her trailer-park revolutionaries in <i>Terminator 2</i>).<br /> <br /> Also, in my write-up, Fetish is a disallowed Background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:43:55-07:00","id":965847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food#post948400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, same goes for all the other breeds. Do they usually use their Crinos form to hunt for food?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think.<br /> It would be unfair against the prey, and as they make a prayer to the spirit of the prey before eating it, it would be kinda problematic.<br /> As for other breeds I think is even less likely. Great cats are even more deadly than wolves but the Bastet Crinos is comparatively less powerful than the Garou Crinos. Corax and Ratkin eat &quot;things&quot; as birds/rats or grab a bite at some cafeteria. Shark is the better hunting form for the Rokea. Nagah, Gurahl and Ajaba try to lurk around even more than other breeds, ad a Crinos hunt would be too much cospicous. Nuwisha probably don't even hunt, they scrounge food from others and the Kitsune generally are too much important (and probably too filthy rich) to even need a non-ritual hunt.<br /> That leaves the Ananasi, that probably like to &quot;play&quot; with their food, thus eating humans while in a shapeshifted -delirium-inducing form because as my humble opinion, they are all inner sadists.<br /> <br /> And of course, BSD and every sort of wyrmfallen shifter hunts in Crinos everything they wants, because they like to be bullies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T03:20:02-07:00","id":968437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/948400-do-werewolf-garou-use-their-crinos-form-to-hunt-for-food?p=965847#post965847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves the Ananasi, that probably like to &quot;play&quot; with their food, thus eating humans while in a shapeshifted -delirium-inducing form because as my humble opinion, they are all inner sadists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, not really. They just don't care much, that's all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually I'd say for Ananasi it doesn't really differ much from other shape-shifters. They'll eat normally in human form if they feel like it or they'll lure and trap or ambush prey in Crawlerling or Pithus form. Also depends on the character in question. An arachnid born Ananasi will probably be more likely to &quot;hunt&quot; on 8 legs (or around a thousand times 8 legs...).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:54:09-07:00","id":983207,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to post a Ron Spencer concept sketch of one of the weredog characters (which will eventually be my cover art), but have been defeated by what I suspect is a bug in the board. I have, however found a workaround:<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Well now,<i> that </i>sure didn't work. Okay, let's try <a href=\"https://uniform-two-six.deviantart.com/art/Tires-Screeching-On-Pavement-701057823\" target=\"_blank\">this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-26-2017, 05:3